# Train Matched Single-Mouse 5 FPS Experiment

This workflow provides a controlled comparison with the dense triplet baseline.
It selects the exact same 800 training and 200 validation source-triplet windows,
then expands each selected window into mouse 0, 1, and 2.

## Experiment Contract

| Property | Dense triplet | Matched single mouse |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Selected source windows | 800 | 800 |
| Resulting mouse trajectories | 2,400 | 2,400 |
| Batch size | 2 triplets | 6 mice |
| Training batches per epoch | 400 | 400 |
| Validation batches per epoch | 100 | 100 |
| Seed | 42 | 42 |

Motion strata are assigned before expansion, so every mouse extracted from a
source window inherits that source window's low, medium, or high label. The
historical independently sampled checkpoint remains unchanged.

## Inspect Configuration

```sh {"id":"01M26SINGLEMOUSEMATCHEDCONFIG","interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.13"}
python src/train.py fit --config src/config/train/flat_dense_single_mouse_matched_5fps.yml --show-config
```

Expected data counts are `train_windows: 2400` and
`validation_windows: 600`.

## Train

```sh {"id":"01M26SINGLEMOUSEMATCHEDTRAIN","interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.13"}
python src/train.py fit --config src/config/train/flat_dense_single_mouse_matched_5fps.yml --wandb
```

The best checkpoint is written to
`checkpoints/flat_dense_single_mouse_matched_5fps/flat_best.pt` and uploaded as
the W&B artifact `flat-dense-single-mouse-matched-5fps-best-checkpoint`.

## Benchmark

Run this after training finishes.

```sh {"id":"01M26SINGLEMOUSEMATCHEDBENCH","interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.13"}
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark/flat_dense_single_mouse_matched_5fps.yml
```

Results are stored under
`outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_single_mouse_matched_5fps/benchmark_16_24/`.
